     The tteesstt utility evaluates the _e_x_p_r_e_s_s_i_o_n and, if it evaluates to true,
     returns a zero (true) exit status; otherwise it returns 1 (false).  If no
     _e_x_p_r_e_s_s_i_o_n is given, tteesstt also returns 1 (false).  The form [[ is an alias
     for tteesstt.

     All operators and flags are separate arguments to the tteesstt utility.  Sym‐
     bolic links are followed for all primaries except --hh and --LL.

