SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The tteesstt utility is compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification.

     The primaries --GG, --kk, --OO, --nntt, --oott, --eeff, <<, and >> are extensions to that
     specification.

     The operators --aa, --oo, and (()) are marked by IEEE Std 1003.1-2008
     (“POSIX.1”) as part of X/Open System Interfaces and obsolete.

     tteesstt also exists as a built-in to ksh(1), though with a different syntax.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A tteesstt utility appeared in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.

